{"resolved":[{"finding":1,"status":"not-resolved","note":"The message history is clamped, but the actual system prompt and tool schemas are not measured; a fixed 1024-token allowance can still under-reserve prompt space and cause context-limit rejection."},{"finding":2,"status":"not-resolved","note":"The regexes are generation-scoped but still overclaim smaller checkpoints: qwen2.5-coder-0.5b and gemma-3-1b match and receive 131072-token windows despite supporting 32768."},{"finding":3,"status":"resolved","note":"Overrides are extracted into applyModelOverrides() and reapplied after refresh() rebuilds the local model entries."},{"finding":4,"status":"resolved","note":"Models classified as embedding-only are skipped during discovery before they can enter the routable chat registry."}],"new_findings":[{"file":"packages/core/src/agent/loop.ts","line":97,"severity":"P1","finding":"computeOutputBudget forces a 256-token minimum even when fewer than 256 tokens remain. For exhausted contexts or small context-window overrides, this guarantees prompt plus requested output exceeds the window and can deterministically reject the request."}]}
